# Clovin Belview, the Abbot's errand-runner and gatekeeper (docs/voice/clovin_belview.md). He meets the party inside
# the abbey gate. He carries St. Markovia's last letter, which he can't read: reading it to him is the key to the
# Abbot's repentance at the unveiling. after: his lines once the Abbot's fate is settled.

~ start
if flag.abbot_fate
-> after
endif
if not flag.clovin_met
set clovin_met
if flag.clovin_met_on_road
Clovin Belview: You! The people from the road. With the wheel. Well. Well, now. Come in out of the wind; it gets up here before anyone else does.
else
Narrator: Inside the gate, a stooped figure in a cast-off monk's habit is sweeping snow into a heap with no particular plan. One of his ears is a hound's. One of his hands is mostly feathers. He looks up and sighs.
Clovin Belview: Visitors. He said there'd be visitors today. He's always right. It's exhausting. Clovin Belview. I open the gate and I carry things.
endif
else
Clovin Belview: You again. Gate's open. Everything's open. The Abbot doesn't believe in locks, except on the wards. He believes in those a great deal.
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* We've come to see the Abbot. -> see_abbot
* Who are the Belviews? -> belviews
* [if not flag.markovia_letter_read] What's that paper you keep touching? -> letter
* [if flag.abbot_bride_revealed] Tell us about the bride. -> bride
* [if flag.abbot_dress_asked and not flag.wedding_dress_found and not flag.wards_dress_found] Where would anyone find a wedding dress up here? -> dress_hint
* [if not flag.clovin_befriended] You look like a man who could use a drink. -> drink
* [if quest.clovins_audience == rumored] The Krezk watch says a Belview came down to their gate to tell a joke. -> krezk/clovins_audience:bucket
* [if flag.clovin_befriended and not quest.clovins_audience] You've gone quiet, Clovin. Something on your mind? -> krezk/clovins_audience:ask
* [if quest.clovins_audience == refused] Dmitri won't open the gate for you. -> krezk/clovins_audience:hood
* [if flag.clovin_family_found] How's your great-uncle? -> krezk/clovins_audience:clovin_after
* Heard anything interesting? -> abbey_of_st_markovia/mothers_ninth_improvement:clovin_news
* Goodbye, Clovin. -> END

~ see_abbot
Clovin Belview: Chapel. North door, the big one. He's in the chapel or he's over in the wards, with her. He doesn't sleep. I've checked. I've checked a lot.
if guest:ireena
Narrator [away]: His hound's ear goes flat as he looks at Ireena. He looks away, and then back, and then away.
Clovin Belview [afraid]: Maybe keep your hood up, miss. In the chapel. He likes red. He likes it too much.
endif
-> menu

~ belviews
Clovin Belview: We were Krezk folk once. Grandmother says. Then we all got sick and came up here and got better. Then he made us better again. And again. He calls it improving.
Clovin Belview: I've had three improvements. You can see two of them. Don't ask about the third. Mother's had nine. She doesn't come out much.
if name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:kip_smudgewick: That's not medicine. I've paid for medicine. It comes in a little bottle, and nobody grows an ear.
else
interject tag:blunt: That's not medicine.
endif
Clovin Belview: No. But he says it with such a kind face.
-> menu

~ letter
Clovin Belview: This? Found it under a loose board in the saint's old room, when I was a lad. Pretty writing. Nobody's ever read it to me. The Abbot says it's nothing. He said it very quickly.
* May we read it to you? -> read_letter
* Keep it safe, Clovin. -> menu

~ read_letter
set markovia_letter_read
Narrator: The paper is old and soft as cloth. The hand is firm, a little hurried, signed with a single M.
Player: "To whoever keeps this house after me. Tomorrow I take the bell-ringers, the gravediggers and the two old soldiers who still remember how, and we go up the road to his door."
Player: "They tell me to reason with him. That he was a prince once and could be again, if someone were patient. I have been patient. Patience is how he feeds."
Player: "Some sicknesses are cured by tenderness. Others only grow fat on it. Keep this house open to the hurt and shut to him. If I do not come back, don't come looking. Light a candle and go on."
Narrator: Clovin is very quiet for a while. His feathered hand opens and closes.
Clovin Belview: She went to kill him. The saint. She didn't go to make friends with him. He told us she went to make friends.
Clovin Belview: Keep it. No. Read it to him. Read it to him when he's happy. I want to see his face.
approve ratatoille +1 liriel_dawnsong +1: You read St. Markovia's letter aloud to Clovin
-> menu

~ bride
Clovin Belview: Vasilka. That's her name; he picked it. I carried half of her up the mountain myself, in a sack, at night, from the graves by the pool. Don't ask which half.
Clovin Belview [sad]: She's very beautiful. That's the worst part. He's very good at it. She'll be the most beautiful thing that ever went down that road, and he'll send her to the castle like a ham.
-> menu

~ dress_hint
Clovin Belview: A dress? Up here? The nuns left in a hurry; they left everything. The matron's room, in the wards, past the cots. It's locked. He locked it. He locks the things he doesn't want to think about.
Clovin Belview: The door sticks. Low down, by the hinge. A good kick and it'd remember it's a door. I didn't tell you that.
-> menu

~ drink
set clovin_befriended
Narrator: From somewhere in his habit he produces a bottle with an inch of wine left in it, and looks at the inch, and at you, and makes a terrible decision.
Clovin Belview: The last of the Martikovs'. Go on. Nobody drinks with me. Mother says it's because of the ear. I say it's because of the wine.
if name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:wren_featherfoot: To the ear. Best ear on the mountain, and I've seen a few today.
else
interject tag:cheerful: To the ear.
endif
Clovin Belview [smile]: To the ear!
approve ratatoille +1 wren_featherfoot +1: You drank the last of the Martikovs' wine with Clovin
-> menu

~ after
if flag.abbot_fate == "repentant"
Clovin Belview: He walked up the mountain at dawn and didn't stop at the top. We all watched. Mother came out to watch. Nobody's going to improve us any more. I keep waiting to be sad.
elif flag.abbot_fate == "slain"
Clovin Belview: You killed him. In his own chapel. I swept up after. There wasn't much; it went to light. Mother says we'll go down to Krezk. Krezk won't have us. We'll go anyway.
elif flag.abbot_fate == "broken"
Clovin Belview: He sits. In the chapel. He doesn't talk. I bring him water and he doesn't drink it, and I take it away and bring more. Somebody has to carry things.
else
Clovin Belview [sad]: I drove her down to the castle. Vasilka. She sat up straight the whole way and asked me what the weather was like at weddings. I said lovely. I'm a liar now. I'm a lot of things.
endif
if flag.markovia_letter_read
Clovin Belview: I've still got the letter. I've learned three of the words. "Light", "candle" and "go". They're good words.
endif
if quest.clovins_audience == rumored or (flag.clovin_befriended and not quest.clovins_audience) or quest.clovins_audience == refused or flag.clovin_family_found or not quest.mothers_ninth_improvement or quest.mothers_ninth_improvement == done
-> krezk/clovins_audience:abbey_menu
endif
-> END
